    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d84">

                <pb facs="0154" n="98" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg98"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/9–444</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President’s Special Assistant</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hopkins</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-09-05">September 5, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: With minor reservations
                    about language which do not affect the intent of the document, “Suggested
                    Recommendations on Treatment of Germany from the Cabinet Committee for the
                        President”,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d84-f1"/> I approve of it.</p>
                <p>If there be agreement on policies, then it becomes of the utmost importance for
                    the proper Government Officials to indicate how the policies in this document
                    are to be implemented.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry L. Hopkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
